<template><main class="privacy-document"><RouterLink to="/">← Back to board</RouterLink><h1>How this board uses data</h1><p>Cueboard is a browser-based planner. The board can run without any Google connection. This notice describes the included code; the operator of a deployed copy is responsible for its hosting and any modifications.</p><h2>Your content stays in this browser</h2><p>Themes, ideas, notes, video links, appearance and YouTube settings are stored in this website origin's IndexedDB browser storage. They are not uploaded to an application server. Hosting providers may process ordinary page-request logs. Exported backups contain your board content, not API keys, tokens or fetched analytics. Browser storage is not encrypted by this app and other scripts sharing this origin can access it.</p><h2>Optional public YouTube connection</h2><p>You supply a YouTube Data API key and channel identifier. The browser sends them directly to Google to request public channel/upload information and public lifetime view, like and comment counts. The key stays in memory unless you select Remember this API key on this device, which stores it in IndexedDB. Forget API key or Disconnect removes that saved key. No key is embedded in the source code or board export.</p><h2>Optional owner connection</h2><p>Google's sign-in library receives your OAuth web client ID and handles sign-in/consent. The board requests YouTube account read-only and YouTube Analytics read-only access. It reads channel identity, upload metadata including scheduled publication times, and period performance reports for public videos you link to ideas. These permissions do not allow uploading, editing or deleting videos. Access tokens stay in memory only; reload or expiry requires reconnection. The code does not request offline access or store refresh tokens.</p><h2>Why reports are saved</h2><p>Upload dates populate the calendar and reports appear alongside your ideas. YouTube API data is used only to display your planning context and performance; the included code does not sell it, share it with advertisers, use it for advertising or train models on it. Dated responses are cached locally for up to 30 days and removed on the next visit or during an open session once expired. Refresh replaces them. YouTube thumbnails may load from <code>i.ytimg.com</code> when you open a calendar preview.</p><h2>Delete data and revoke access</h2><p>Clear saved YouTube data removes cached uploads and reports without changing the board. Disconnect removes the session token and any saved API key; dated cached reports remain until cleared or expired. Revoke Google access clears the cache and requests revocation of the current token. You can remove authorization at any time using <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Account connections</a>, including when the local token has expired. Clear this website's browser site data to remove all local board content and settings. Export a backup first if you want to keep your ideas.</p><h2>Google and deployment information</h2><p>Use of the YouTube integration is subject to <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>. API calls go directly to Google's services. This template has no shared backend, developer API key or verified shared OAuth client. Each deployment operator should provide their own contact details and privacy information before offering a shared service.</p><footer><RouterLink to="/">Back to board</RouterLink> · See the repository README for setup.</footer></main></template>
